Subject: [PATCH 0445/1695] drivers: scmi_msg: fix size_t trace format

Fix format specifier for size_t type argument.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 591f863e5752be215d4dab04ff9e9b3325a8ab54 drivers: scmi_msg: fix size_t trace format]
Change-Id: I62ecbd07ad5422d2d62fa2e17cb8766fd0f3eb92
Signed-off-by: Etienne Carriere <etienne.carriere@foss.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/scmi-msg/smt.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/scmi-msg/smt.c b/core/drivers/scmi-msg/smt.c
index 880212bef..8067f66c5 100644
--- a/core/drivers/scmi-msg/smt.c
+++ b/core/drivers/scmi-msg/smt.c
@@ -97,7 +97,7 @@ void scmi_entry_smt(unsigned int channel_id, uint32_t *payload_buf)
 			  sizeof(smt_hdr->message_header);
 
 	if (in_payload_size > SCMI_SEC_PAYLOAD_SIZE) {
-		DMSG("SCMI payload too big %u", in_payload_size);
+		DMSG("SCMI payload too big %zu", in_payload_size);
 		goto out;
 	}
 
